'''Estret''' ({{lang|ca|Estret}}, from Volisanian ''estret'' "narrow, strait") is the easternmost and most populous [[Provinces of Balboa|province]] of [[Balboa]]. Located on the narrowest portion of the [[Balboa isthmus]], it is bordered by [[Jala Province]] to the northwest and [[Migjorn Province]] to the south, with the [[Aethiopian Ocean]] to the east and the [[Shendan Ocean]] to the west. The province has an area of 20,600 km² and a population of approximately 14.5 million (2026 estimate), making it the smallest but most densely populated province in the country. The provincial capital is [[Sant Cristòfor]], which is also the national capital and the largest city in Balboa.

The [[International City of Areza]], a permanently neutral international district on [[Lake Alvarado]] within the [[Balboa Canal]] zone, forms an enclave within Estret Province but is not subject to Balboan sovereignty. Areza is the seat of the [[Adonian Community Assembly]] and several other AC institutions.

Estret is the economic centre of Balboa, containing the country's principal financial district, the Balboa Canal's Shendan terminus at [[Portnou]], the [[Sant Cristòfor Free Trade Zone]], and the majority of the nation's logistics and transshipment infrastructure. The province accounts for approximately 41 per cent of the national population and a disproportionate share of GDP.

== Geography ==

[[File:Serralada d'Estret from Estany de Panacú.png|thumb|right|300px|The Serralada d'Estret as seen from the Estany de Panacú, with the lake's basin in the foreground.]]

Estret occupies the narrowest portion of the Balboa isthmus, where the [[Yalabirga Mountain Range]] dips to its lowest elevation. The [[Serralada d'Estret]] (Estret Hills), the local name for the Yalabirga in this region, reaches elevations of no more than 250 metres and forms the watershed divide between the Shendan (western) and Aethiopian (eastern) coastal plains. The low crossing made this the natural corridor for interoceanic transit long before the canal, and it remains the most strategically significant stretch of the isthmus.

The province is divided between two coastal plains. The Shendan coastal plain, which faces west, contains the city of Sant Cristòfor — whose growth was driven by the sheltered anchorage of the [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]] — the canal terminus at [[Portnou]], and the majority of the province's urban population; it is narrower and drier, lying in the rain shadow of the Serralada d'Estret. The Aethiopian coastal plain, which faces east, is broader and wetter; it contains the naval base at Haicang, the exurbs of Baix Llevant, and a string of rural comarcas.

The major rivers of the province all originate in the Serralada d'Estret or the [[Estany de Panacú]] basin. On the Shendan side, the [[Riu Burutí]], [[Riu Besòs]], [[Riu Llobregat]], [[Riu Segre]], [[Riu Ter]], and [[Riu Fluvià]] flow westward to the Shendan coast. On the Aethiopian side, the [[Riu Ebre]] and [[Riu Francolí]] flow eastward. The [[Estany de Panacú]], a large natural lake in the interior, is the source of the Riu Segre and the centrepiece of the inland comarca of [[L'Estany (comarca)|L'Estany]].

[[Lake Alvarado]], an artificial lake created by the damming of the canal corridor, occupies the southern portion of the province between the comarcas of [[Marjal del Canal]], [[Cumará]], and [[Baix Llevant]]. [[Lake Jarumá]], a natural lake near the northeast corner of Marjal del Canal, is a smaller freshwater body.

The [[Badia de Sant Cristòfor]] (Bay of Sant Cristòfor) is a large bay on the Shendan coast, sheltered by the [[Península de la Barceloneta]] and containing three major islands: [[Illa del Portal]], [[Illa Daurada]], and [[Illa de Matarí]]. On the Aethiopian coast, the [[Badia del Ferro]] (Iron Bay) at Haicang provides a natural harbour for the Balboan navy.

The [[Illes del Guano]], an archipelago of five islands off the Aethiopian coast, form a separate comarca. The largest island, [[Illa de Tamaní]] (562 km²), is the only one with significant permanent settlement.

=== Climate ===

Estret has a tropical climate, with a wet season from May to December and a dry season from January to April. The Aethiopian coast receives higher rainfall than the Shendan coast, which lies in the rain shadow of the Serralada d'Estret. Average annual rainfall ranges from approximately 1,600 mm on the Aethiopian coast to 900 mm on the Shendan coast. Temperatures are consistently warm, with average highs of 30–32 °C and average lows of 22–24 °C throughout the year; the interior basin around the Estany de Panacú is slightly cooler due to elevation.

=== Flora and fauna ===

{{main|Wildlife of Balboa}}

[[File:Parc Nacional de les Illes mangroves.png|thumb|right|300px|Mangrove forests in the Parc Nacional de les Illes, off the Shendan coast.]]

The Aethiopian coastal lowlands support tropical dry forest and mangrove ecosystems, particularly in the estuarine zones of the major rivers. The mangrove forests of the Estret coast are among the most extensive on the isthmus and serve as critical nursery habitat for commercially important fish and crustacean species. The Shendan coast, which lies in the rain shadow of the Yalabirga, supports drier tropical forest and thorn-scrub habitats.

The coastal wetlands of the [[Els Aiguamolls]] comarca are a significant ecological area, designated as the [[Parc Nacional de les Illes]] on the offshore islands of [[Illa de Siburí]] and [[Illa de Yarumí]]. The [[Illa del Portal]], formerly a quarantine station, is now a nature reserve. The Illes del Guano, formerly exploited for guano mining, are now largely nature reserves supporting large seabird colonies.

Lake Alvarado and its associated wetlands form a significant freshwater ecosystem, supporting large populations of waterfowl and wading birds. The Estany de Panacú supports a resident fish community and is a recreational fishery.

